    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0332" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1866: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-03T16:00:00+03:25">May 3, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—9:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. My number 134. Kuniholm reports as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>May 2, 2 p.m. Soviet Consul General, commanding officer Red troops,
                            Iranian officials, and Kurds have met at Askerabad village near Rezaieh.
                            Kurds have resented [<hi rendition="#italic">presented</hi>] series of
                            demands which must be discussed further at Tehran as well as by
                            Russians. Soviet Consul General has appealed to Kurds to disband and go
                            home. Kurdish depredations continue.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
